# Demo server - tools/server documentation. Sources: UI.md, EDITOR.md, ANNOTATIONS.md,
# YAMLOVER_EDITOR.yo, QUERY_EDITOR.yo - progress in ../../DOCSMIGRATION.md.
Demo server
description: the yamlover web server - the UI, the projectional editors and their state machines, annotations
- >
  `tools/server` (`npx yamlover <root>`) serves a web app that browses a yamlover project as a
  graph of nodes and edits it **in place**. This chapter is its documentation: [operating the
  UI](::server:ui) is the user-facing guide, [the projectional editor](::server:editor) is the
  maintainer's architecture map, and [annotations](::server:annotations) covers fragments and
  tagging. The editors' behavior is specified state by state in three machine chapters - [the
  yamlover editor](::server:yamlover-editor) (the source projection's typing grammar), [the
  chapter editor](::server:chapter-editor) (the prose projection), and [the query
  editor](::server:query-editor) (the breadcrumb, pointer cells, and tag picker) - each state a
  subchapter, its transitions a table of links.
- >
  This documentation is dogfood: the book you are reading is served by the very server it
  describes, and these machine chapters were edited with the editors they specify.
- *: ui
- *: editor
- *: yamlover-editor
- *: chapter-editor
- *: query-editor
- *: annotations
